BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Association of Health Care Journalists' Health Journalism Conferen
 ce '26
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260527T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260530T000000
UID:192113c94f69cd7d17b3b192ff526ffd@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Minneapolis\, Minnesota\, United States\nJoin the Association 
 of Health Care Journalists in Minneapolis for several days of field trips\
 , sessions and networking opportunities. Be sure to mark your calendar for
  the hands-on workshop "Covering Health Disparities From a Solutions Journ
 alism Lens" with Nora Hertel\, executive director of Project Optimist\, an
 d SJN's Wilson Liévano. You'll learn how to recognize leads that can turn
  into solutions stories and how to apply solutions journalism's four pilla
 rs framework. The workshop will be on May 28 from 8:30 a.m. to 10:00 a.m.
LOCATION:Minneapolis\, Minnesota\, United States
URL:https://healthjournalism.org/training-events/health-journalism-2026/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Groundswell
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260603T000000
UID:79b794dad624e73be8cca83f6e6252b2@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Dehradun\, India\nSJN is excited to partner with The Migration
  Story for the inaugural Groundswell. Happening in Dehradun\, India\, June
  2 and 3\, this gathering will bring together nonprofits\, community group
 s\, think tanks\, research organizations\, journalists and government repr
 esentatives for a massive exploration of narrative and solutions. How can 
 we tell a more constructive\, more nuanced story of migration? And how can
  migrants themselves be participants in storytelling and solutions? Regist
 ration is open.
LOCATION:Dehradun\, India
URL:https://themigrationstory.com/post/come-to-groundswell/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:⭐ APPLY NOW: Train-the-Trainers (July 2026 Cohort)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T000000
UID:fa17565b28f84d4130002c848d07dcce@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nA new round of the SJN’s Train-the-Trainers program 
 is open now. For those accepted\, you’ll get extensive solutions journal
 ism training over the course of five sessions in July. That training will 
 deeply cover the fundamentals of solutions journalism before exploring bes
 t practices in teaching and training others in it.\nThe hosts for this rou
 nd will be Kyuwon Lee and Sharon Bloyd-Peshkin\, SJN's Training & Curricul
 um Managers\, and Raoul Junior Lorfils\, an accredited trainer in Haiti an
 d Canada. We'll also be joined by multiple SJN staff members and accomplis
 hed trainers from our network\, who will provide insight into their work i
 n solutions journalism. The deadline to apply is June 7\, soget all the de
 tails\, timing\, requirements and the full application all in one place.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQVupQXrW1bCkdvveBHVJyPmz6Ra
 VtG69TQDnKLtPHKZuVIA/viewform
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
